//! The development-host seam: handing the process to a `zeli serve` host that
//! loads the app as a shared image and loads a new one on every edit.
//!
//! It is deliberately its own module. Reaching this through `std:zeus` would
//! compile the whole engine into the *host* program — and the engine belongs to
//! the image the host loads, so the host would carry a second, divergent copy
//! that any unrouted call could quietly land in. Importing this pulls in nothing
//! else.

/// Hand the process to the host that loads the app image at `path`. On every
/// target but a host one this does nothing: the program runs its own loop.
fn run(path: string) {}
